    "scope": "D3D9 additional swap chains now use the existing supported render-target multisampling/resolve path, forwarding the requested sample type and validated quality to storage instead of refusing every nonzero type or silently creating NONE. Unsupported sample modes still fail before allocation/emission; cached parameters/Surface.GetDesc and capability quality-level metadata agree. Shared D3D8/9 SDK probes both construct 4x additional buffers, retain them through 32 public-zero chain revivals per API and present two exact colors, then perform binding-only Reset/private-object cleanup. Independent replay validates actual four-sample GPU attachment pixels through a separate explicit resolve, the host resolved texture and displayed scanout. Structural MSAA/flag/quality guards from 8b remain unchanged. Update the older manual MSAA SDK to expect the newly supported D3D9 additional case; the immutable 8b fixture preserves historical unsupported behavior. Full MSAA/format/depth compatibility, refresh/fullscreen validation, multiple-buffer storage/rotation, standalone target counts, complete Reset/thread/device loss, original Microsoft HAL, games/FPS and review stages 4/5/6 remain incomplete. No host/protocol/shader/bundle change.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "file": "d3d8-com-swapchain.c",
        "blobSha1": "433da09d04b830ee37fdb591cfce7aa207f95033",
        "sha256": "ec08bb0c41b251d542086be03d1d0d445dc3ba73eda4d51c4f585e55f6ab6d90",
        "url": "https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/415a275e3844c252ad385b46023095e9401ca234/dlls/d3d8/swapchain.c",
        "evidence": "Pinned implementation AddRef from public zero acquires a parent device and physical swap-chain storage reference; Release to zero drops these references. Public surface references retain the same physical chain. This is implementation evidence for valid zero-count revival while storage survives, not a claim that repeated zero-count D3D8 chain Release is a native API guarantee."
      },
      {
        "file": "d3d8-container-surface.c",
        "sha256": "94409282de3533f8ddfe4392c04568346d090bb5f39f1bb33fef910613e13f89",
        "blobSha1": "5b02035d53980c006fc19122b028f9263d1219a5",
        "url": "https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/415a275e3844c252ad385b46023095e9401ca234/dlls/d3d8/surface.c",
        "evidence": "Surface AddRef/Release maintain their own resource.refcount for non-texture public surfaces; device and underlying texture/swapchain references change only on public zero/nonzero edges. Release storage before the parent device, since storage destruction can free the surface."
      },
      {
        "file": "d3d9-device-tests.c",
        "sha256": "78c0925be01fba6e2b3ce54a7f6f9f32e2a3c3d0680b48eabb102b00d50c89eb",
